> That is a serious contractual hurdle, but not necessarily the final word. Because this involves consumer work on a **Pennsylvania residence**, Pennsylvania may have strong mandatory protections that cannot be waived by a California choice-of-law clause—especially rules governing home-improvement contracts, contractor registration, cancellation rights, deceptive practices, and remedies.
